message: "If you use this software or benchmark in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Big Data Technologies (BDT): Real-Time IoT Anomaly Detection with Apache Flink"
abstract: "Big Data Technologies (BDT) is a course project demonstrating real-time IoT anomaly detection with Apache Kafka and Apache Flink. Isolation Forest, Autoencoder, and XGBoost ONNX models run in the Flink JVM, with results stored in ClickHouse and Redis and shown in a live dashboard. In one local 40,000-event replay, the fast Isolation Forest plus Autoencoder baseline achieved F1 0.4125 at 1,283 events per second; selective XGBoost escalation achieved F1 0.8238 at 1,332 events per second, escalating 20.51 percent of events. These are single-run, local measurements under burst input; the optional Laya comparison is experimental."
